module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_empty_controls_report_reads_as_all_held

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data an_empty_controls_report_reads_as_all_held: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_empty_controls_report_reads_as_all_held" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the capability of a controls instrument reporting a three-valued outcome per declared control identity (held, refused with its failure text, no verdict), joined by identity against one declared roster, so that a control that produced nothing has no constructor that reads as held" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_controls_report is a concatenation of control outputs, and roster_import_sweep_controls_wire reads an EMPTY report as success. A control signals held by contributing the empty string and failure by contributing CONTROL-FAIL text, so HELD is the ABSENCE of text, never a positive per-control result. A control that contributed nothing because it did not run, was removed from the concatenation, or returned early on an unexpected path is indistinguishable from one that held.",
    "POPULATION, EXACT (read at main 6b9fa5e6 by parsing the report's invocations, not by count): 110 distinct leaf controls. 61 sit in the four groups (rename 25, disjoint 10, occ 21, head 5) that roster_rename_control_count_check joins by identity against roster_rename_control_names; 49 have no identity join: the 33 top-level terms of roster_controls_report (24 taking the prepared grammar, 9 not) and the 16 terms of roster_kind_controls. Sub-checks inside a leaf (relocation-splice checks a good and a stale-head case) are not counted as leaves.",
    "SOURCE REPRODUCER (the shape, stated as source; not executed here; E denotes the empty string, F a CONTROL-FAIL line): `fn checks(x: Int) -> String { if x == 1 { E } else { F } }`, `fn silent(x: Int) -> String { E }`, `fn report(ok: Bool) -> String { if ok { checks(x: 1) + silent(x: 2) } else { F } }`, and the wire rule `if report == E { ExitSuccess } else { exit_failure(reason: report) }`. POSITIVE CONTROL: checks(x: 1) is a real held control and contributes E. COUNTEREXAMPLES, each reading exactly as that positive control does: (a) EMPTY: a report with zero terms is E and exits success; (b) SILENT: silent(x: 2) never checks its input and contributes E; (c) DELETED: removing a term from the concatenation leaves the report E. (d) REJECTED PREPARATION is the one case the shape does surface, as a single F for every control at once, which names no control and cannot say which ran. No arm of the report type distinguishes (a), (b) or (c) from the positive control; that is the invalid state.",
    "COUNTED GROUPS ARE NOT SAFE EITHER, BY SOURCE READING: roster_rename_control_names declares 57 names but the four counted groups invoke 61; occurrences-keyed-pipe-site-rewrites, occurrences-keyed-negated-pipe-site-rewrites, occurrences-keyed-chained-pipe-refuses-not-skips and occurrences-keyed-non-head-reference-refuses-arity (all four added to roster_occ_controls by #15474, 719550dd, without a matching declaration) run undeclared, so the count check should emit four 'ran an undeclared control' lines and a count line. This is SOURCE-PREDICTED, NOT EXECUTED: of the receipts surveyed (srv2 hb-base at cb97d81c and hb-cand at fcb6c883, 2026-11-03) neither completed the label, both timing out at 3600s. The bookkeeping repair is #15721 (the four names declared; an executed static identity check over the source shows 61 invoked, 61 declared). That repair leaves the 49 unjoined leaves and this row's class untouched. The hand-written name list is the second authority the identity roster below removes.",
    "HARM: //gunbc/instruments:roster-import-sweep-controls is admission evidence for NAMESPACE-XL sweep waves. Every green reading of it is POTENTIALLY UNSOUND for the 49 uncounted leaves until a run reports a positive per-leaf result: a deleted or silent control among them leaves the label green with no signal. The label stays enrolled, but enrollment is not evidence that its green is sound. Same class as gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_cost_probe_reports_pass_on_a_rejected_input, and it stands on the reproducer above, not on that analogy.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (silent: no output and held produce the same empty report and the same exit 0). Found by reading during the per-control inventory for the option (b) split design of the controls label (wise-moth-707 for tidy-ant-251, approved for local authoring by keen-otter-392, 2026-11-03). No instance of a dropped or silent control among the 49 is claimed; the claim is that one would not be seen.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. One declared roster of control identities from which every entry structure is derived; each run yields a POSITIVE typed result per identity: HELD { identity } | CONTROL-FAIL { identity, text } | NO-VERDICT { identity, cause }. The aggregate is green only when every declared identity is HELD; a missing, duplicated or undeclared identity refuses; CONTROL-FAIL and NO-VERDICT stay separate per leaf, so an incomplete run never hides a known failing control; a rejected preparation is NO-VERDICT for each identity, never a single unnamed line. The rename group's count check is the existing local instance to generalise, not a second mechanism beside it.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY: the per-identity typed outcome above, over the whole label, with the roster checked against the declared controls and their invocations independently enough to catch a leaf the roster omits. NOT satisfied by extending roster_rename_control_names by hand while the report stays a string concatenation, which narrows this instance and leaves the class.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_controls_report", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_import_sweep_controls_wire", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_rename_control_count_check", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
